::ALG1_U02_L01_Quiz_Q23::
Question ID: ALG1_U02_L01_Q23
MLA Standard: No new primary MLA standard; prerequisite support.
Question:
Solve -6a = 42.
{
=A. a = -7#Divide both sides by -6, and 42 divided by -6 is -7.
~B. a = 7#This has the wrong sign because a positive divided by a negative is negative.
~C. a = -252#This multiplies instead of dividing by -6.
~D. a = 36#This subtracts 6 instead of undoing multiplication.
}

